  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while the encoder, windows, and decoder remain a straight flow.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense carrier, so the spatial output has something persistent to update. Windowing partitions that field before the thought process starts. The shared DQ-CTM parameters repeat across ticks, so the loop returns only to the thought stage. The decoder reads the updated dense carrier after the ticks finish.",
      "evidence": [
