    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation separates dense feature construction from window partitioning while preserving the tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field. That field is the persistent carrier the compact thought process can read and update. Window partitioning produces tokens from the carrier rather than discarding the carrier. The equation keeps the dense field and the windowed tokens as separate objects.",
